00:00:42.631 --> 00:00:44.847
Alright so coming at number five,

00:00:44.847 --> 00:00:48.164
is The Power of Broke by Daymond John.

00:00:48.164 --> 00:00:50.836
(guitar music)

00:00:50.836 --> 00:00:53.191
- This book is called The Power of Broke,

00:00:53.191 --> 00:00:54.160
and when you open the book

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.997
the first thing you read is

00:00:55.997 --> 00:00:58.564
"The power of broke is a mindset.

00:00:58.564 --> 00:01:00.070
"It exist in all of us,

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.233
"whether we have money,
opportunities or advantages.

00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:05.255
"Trouble is, most people
don't recognize the power

00:01:05.255 --> 00:01:06.553
"for what it is.

00:01:06.553 --> 00:01:07.489
"They leave it alone,

00:01:07.489 --> 00:01:10.070
"or maybe they don't
even know it's there."

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.367
What is the power of broke?

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:12.429
What do you mean by that?

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:13.262
- That's that hunger.

00:01:13.262 --> 00:01:14.095
That's that drive.

00:01:14.095 --> 00:01:17.153
That's that instinct that nothing
is ever going to stop you.

00:01:17.153 --> 00:01:21.218
Listen, I'm not sitting
there saying that to be broke

00:01:21.218 --> 00:01:23.252
and not have those resources
to feed your family

00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:25.851
and get great medical attention

00:01:25.851 --> 00:01:27.563
is something we should celebrate.

00:01:27.563 --> 00:01:30.018
I'm not saying that by far.

00:01:30.018 --> 00:01:30.851
But I'm saying that,

00:01:30.851 --> 00:01:32.794
if you're going to be in a situation

00:01:32.794 --> 00:01:35.782
where you don't have the
things that you want in life

00:01:35.782 --> 00:01:37.098
and you're hungry,

00:01:37.098 --> 00:01:39.478
then that's the situation,
let's tap into it.

00:01:39.478 --> 00:01:42.501
And the people that I see
utilize The Power of Broke,

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:46.205
more than anybody at
all, are the people that

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.949
when they reach a level of
success they still use it

00:01:48.949 --> 00:01:51.507
and that's how they
maintain their success.

00:01:51.507 --> 00:01:52.827
That hunger and drive.

00:01:52.827 --> 00:01:55.491
And we grow up at a time
and age where it was,

00:01:55.491 --> 00:01:58.172
you need money to make money,
you got to know somebody.

00:01:58.172 --> 00:02:00.216
Well, you know, I mean look at me.

00:02:00.216 --> 00:02:01.540
Look at half this room.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:05.081
I grew up African
American, short, dyslexic,

00:02:05.081 --> 00:02:08.363
got left back one time, almost
got left back a second time,

00:02:08.363 --> 00:02:10.938
can't dribble a basketball, can't sing,

00:02:10.938 --> 00:02:12.989
can't draw, didn't know anybody,

00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:14.384
didn't go to college,

00:02:14.384 --> 00:02:16.524
that didn't stop me at all, right?

00:02:16.524 --> 00:02:18.521
I had a mother that really loved me dearly

00:02:18.521 --> 00:02:21.769
and I had some like-minded
frugal partners and friends,

00:02:21.769 --> 00:02:22.949
who would never let me stop

00:02:22.949 --> 00:02:24.352
and I never let them stop,

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:25.971
and I had a will and a drive

00:02:25.971 --> 00:02:28.295
and I still have all those same things.

00:02:28.295 --> 00:02:30.461
I still rise and grind
every single morning.

00:02:30.461 --> 00:02:34.132
You see me in a suit on TV
handing out millions of dollars.

00:02:34.132 --> 00:02:37.607
Looking like another just
buttoned up executive.

00:02:37.607 --> 00:02:39.407
But it wasn't always like that.

00:02:39.407 --> 00:02:41.537
You see, I had a secret tool.

00:02:41.537 --> 00:02:44.958
It was there for me when
I had absolutely nothing.

00:02:44.958 --> 00:02:46.876
When I thought I was nothing.

00:02:46.876 --> 00:02:49.759
Until it lead me to everything.

00:02:49.759 --> 00:02:52.193
You may think it's your biggest weakness.

00:02:52.193 --> 00:02:53.923
But if you wield it properly,

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:57.560
it will definitely be
the key to your success.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.810
This is The Power of Broke.

00:03:02.259 --> 00:03:03.986
- You tell me you couldn't be authentic,

00:03:03.986 --> 00:03:06.296
or original, or come up with some concept.

00:03:06.296 --> 00:03:07.761
No matter what you have,

00:03:07.761 --> 00:03:09.761
there's enough to do it.

00:03:11.088 --> 00:03:14.291
- Broke can break you or
give you immense energy.

00:03:14.291 --> 00:03:16.809
If you're someone that refuses to lose,

00:03:16.809 --> 00:03:18.907
it's going to give you
all the fuel you need

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:21.484
to continue to push further.

00:03:21.484 --> 00:03:22.808
- The level of rejection,

00:03:22.808 --> 00:03:25.441
and the height to which
we're trying to aspire to

00:03:25.441 --> 00:03:29.024
at times feels so
insurmountable and crazy.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.244
- The people who are in
a position to buy my book

00:03:33.244 --> 00:03:35.142
where not my target audience,

00:03:35.142 --> 00:03:38.059
and so it didn't register for them.

00:03:39.317 --> 00:03:41.091
- One of my favorite sayings is,

00:03:41.091 --> 00:03:44.091
"Try, fail, try again, fail better."

00:03:45.684 --> 00:03:47.294
- Being without capital

00:03:47.294 --> 00:03:49.426
is one of the greatest gifts you can have

00:03:49.426 --> 00:03:51.593
if you're an entrepreneur.

00:03:52.773 --> 00:03:54.409
- Capital isn't the most
important ingredient

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:55.450
for business any more.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.117
It's now creativity and passion.

00:03:59.279 --> 00:04:00.375
- And I want people to believe

00:04:00.375 --> 00:04:02.425
that they can actually be
whatever they want to be.

00:04:02.425 --> 00:04:03.541
Do whatever they want to do.

00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:05.063
And really the sky's the limit.

00:04:05.063 --> 00:04:06.896
You know, it's people.

